        "section": "lie-groups",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "SU(2) and SO(3) - Double Cover, Spinors, Angular Momentum",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "SU(2) and SO(3) have the same Lie algebra but are different groups. SU(2) is a 2-to-1 cover\nof SO(3). The two sheets correspond to integer-spin vs half-integer-spin representations. This\nis not a mathematical technicality — it is the reason fermions exist."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-SU2-SO3.md#003",
      "path": [
        "04-SU2-SO3.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:lie-groups:04-su2-so3, git-history:lie-groups:04-su2-so3]",
        "canonical_path": "lie-groups/04-SU2-SO3.md",
        "concepts": "[su2, so3]",
        "current_path": "lie-groups/04-SU2-SO3.md",
        "id": "maxim:lie-groups:su2-so3",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "lie-groups",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[su2, so3]",
        "section": "lie-groups",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "SU(2) and SO(3) - Double Cover, Spinors, Angular Momentum",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+----------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|             THE SU(2) -> SO(3) DOUBLE COVER                          |\n+----------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                                                                      |\n|   SU(2) = S^3 ⊂ C^2                  SO(3) = RP^3                  |\n|   unit quaternions                     rotation matrices             |\n|   dim = 3, simply connected            pi_1 = Z/2Z                  |\n|   center = {I, -I} = Z_2              center = {I}                  |\n|                                                                      |\n|         phi: SU(2) --2-to-1--> SO(3)                                |\n|              {A, -A}  |-------> same rotation                        |\n|                                                                      |\n|   REPRESENTATIONS:                                                   |\n|   SU(2) irreps:  j = 0, 1/2, 1, 3/2, 2, ...  (all half-integers)   |\n|   SO(3) irreps:  j = 0, 1, 2, ...             (integers only)       |\n|                                                                      |\n|   Half-integer j reps: lift to SU(2) but NOT to SO(3)               |\n|   Integer j reps: descend to SO(3)                                   |\n|                                                                      |\n|   SPINORS = the j=1/2 representation of SU(2)                       |\n|   A 2pi rotation sends a spinor to its negative.                     |\n|   A 4pi rotation is the identity.                                    |\n|                                                                      |\n+----------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
