      },
      "text": "## SO(3) Explicitly"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-SU2-SO3.md#013",
      "path": [
        "04-SU2-SO3.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:lie-groups:04-su2-so3, git-history:lie-groups:04-su2-so3]",
        "canonical_path": "lie-groups/04-SU2-SO3.md",
        "concepts": "[su2, so3]",
        "current_path": "lie-groups/04-SU2-SO3.md",
        "id": "maxim:lie-groups:su2-so3",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "lie-groups",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[su2, so3]",
        "section": "lie-groups",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "SU(2) and SO(3) - Double Cover, Spinors, Angular Momentum",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "SO(3) = 3x3 real orthogonal matrices with det = +1. Every element is a rotation:\n```\nAbout z-axis by angle theta:\nR_z(theta) = [[cos theta, -sin theta, 0],\n              [sin theta,  cos theta, 0],\n              [0,          0,         1]]"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-SU2-SO3.md#014",
      "path": [
        "04-SU2-SO3.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:lie-groups:04-su2-so3, git-history:lie-groups:04-su2-so3]",
        "canonical_path": "lie-groups/04-SU2-SO3.md",
        "concepts": "[su2, so3]",
        "current_path": "lie-groups/04-SU2-SO3.md",
        "id": "maxim:lie-groups:su2-so3",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "lie-groups",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[su2, so3]",
        "section": "lie-groups",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "SU(2) and SO(3) - Double Cover, Spinors, Angular Momentum",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "General rotation by angle theta about unit axis n:\nR(n,theta) = I + sin(theta) N + (1-cos theta) N^2    (Rodrigues' formula)\nwhere N = [[0,-n_3,n_2],[n_3,0,-n_1],[-n_2,n_1,0]] is the cross-product matrix.\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-SU2-SO3.md#015",
      "path": [
        "04-SU2-SO3.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:lie-groups:04-su2-so3, git-history:lie-groups:04-su2-so3]",
        "canonical_path": "lie-groups/04-SU2-SO3.md",
        "concepts": "[su2, so3]",
        "current_path": "lie-groups/04-SU2-SO3.md",
        "id": "maxim:lie-groups:su2-so3",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "lie-groups",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[su2, so3]",
        "section": "lie-groups",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "SU(2) and SO(3) - Double Cover, Spinors, Angular Momentum",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Topology:** SO(3) iso RP^3. Every rotation is specified by (axis n, angle theta) with theta in [0,pi]\nand the identification (n, pi) ~ (-n, pi). The fundamental group pi_1(SO(3)) = Z/2Z — the nontrivial\nloop is a 2pi rotation. A 2pi rotation is NOT homotopic to the identity; a 4pi rotation IS."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-SU2-SO3.md#016",
      "path": [
        "04-SU2-SO3.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:lie-groups:04-su2-so3, git-history:lie-groups:04-su2-so3]",
        "canonical_path": "lie-groups/04-SU2-SO3.md",
        "concepts": "[su2, so3]",
        "current_path": "lie-groups/04-SU2-SO3.md",
        "id": "maxim:lie-groups:su2-so3",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "lie-groups",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[su2, so3]",
        "section": "lie-groups",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "SU(2) and SO(3) - Double Cover, Spinors, Angular Momentum",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "This is demonstrable physically with the **Dirac belt trick** (or Philippine wine dance): attach\none end of a belt to a cup, make a 2pi rotation, and the belt is twisted with no untwisting possible\nwithout further rotation. Make a 4pi rotation and you can untwist."
    },
